{"id":"word:hebrew:H3092","type":"word","title":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","subtitle":"H3092 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Jehoshaphat , the name of six Israelites; also of a valley near Jerusalem","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יְהוֹשָׁפָט (H3092) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m n-pr-loc.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 84 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט (Yᵉhôwshâphâṭ) means Jehoshaphat , the name of six Israelites; also of a valley near Jerusalem First listed occurrence: 1Chr 3 10."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","transliteration":"Yᵉhôwshâphâṭ","pronunciation":"yeh-ho-shaw-fawt'","strong":"H3092","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3092","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m n-pr-loc","forms":["יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט","יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט","יְהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט","יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט","יְהֽוֹשָׁפָט֙"],"morphs":[["HNp",67],["HC/Np",11],["HR/Np",6]]},"definitions":{"short":"Jehoshaphat , the name of six Israelites; also of a valley near Jerusalem","usage":"Jehoshaphat. Compare 3146 .","full":"H3092. Yehoshaphat יוֺשָׁפָט יְהוֺשָׁפָט, proper name, masculine ᵐ5 Ἰωσαφαθ , Ἰωσαφατ ( ׳י hath judged , compare שְׁפַטְיָהוּ אֱלִישָׁפָט, & references) — 1 ׳יְהוֺ (so all except 5 & 6 ) king of Judah, son of Asa 1Kin 15:24 ; 22:2 21 t. 1Kings; 2Kin 1:17 ; 3:1 , 7 , 11 , 12 (twice in verse); 3:14 ; 8:16 (twice in verse); 12:19 ; 1Chr 3:10 ; 2Chr 17:1 40t. 2 Chronicles. 2 father of Jehu king of Israel 2Kin 9:2 , 14 . 3 chronicler under David & Solomon, son of Ahilud 2Sam 8:16 ; 1Kin 4:3 ; 1Chr 18:15 ; also 2Sam 20:24 ( ᵐ5 L Σαφαν ). 4 one of Solomon's 12 officers who provided victuals for the royal household 1Kin 4:17 ( ᵐ5 L Ἰωασαφατ ). 5 ׳יוֺ one of David's heroes 1Chr 11:43 . 6 ׳יוֺ a priest & trumpeter in David's time 1Chr 15:24 . 7 in proper name, of a location יְהוֺשָׁפָט עֵמֶק Joel 1Chr 4:2 , 12 , symbolical name of a valley near Jerusalem, place of ultimate judgement.","rootNote":"fr